{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1197007","title":"GHG emissions from  algal-bacterial granules","description":"This study aimed to investigate N2O emission characteristics and its mitigation potential using photosynthetically reduced carbon dioxide (CO2). With increasing Chlorophyll-a contents (0-13.4 mg/g-MLVSS), N2O emission factors largely fluctuated within 0.4-3.0%, but uncorrelated with algae contents. The photosynthetically reduced CO2 emissions were positively correlated (R2=0.88) with Chlorophyll-a contents, and it can offset average N2O emissions (1.4%) when Chlorophyll-a achieved 11.1 mg/g-MLVSS. However, the algal-bacterial granules underwent disintegration twice due to decreasing CO2 availability, which indicated that Cyanobacteria-dominated granules can retain higher Chlorophyll-a content compared to Chlorophyta-dominated granules.","center":"Shanghai Academy of Environmental Sciences","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2024/12/11 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN45771088","Sludge","uncertain",null,"2023-11-27",2023,null,null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,null,"reactor sample",null,null,null,"environmental sample; urban association not established"],["SAMN45771089","Sludge","uncertain",null,"2023-11-27",2023,null,null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,null,"reactor sample",null,null,null,"environmental sample; urban association not established"],["SAMN45771090","Sludge","uncertain",null,"2023-11-27",2023,null,null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,null,"reactor sample",null,null,null,"environmental sample; urban association not established"],["SAMN45771091","Sludge","uncertain",null,"2023-11-27",2023,null,null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,null,"reactor sample",null,null,null,"environme